1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
These tabs ship with sample rows in their yellow cells. Replace them with yours.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:12,000
Sinking funds set aside a little each check for costs you know are coming.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:20,500
Type each fund's yearly cost, when it is due, and what is saved so far.

4
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:28,000
The sheet shows how much to set aside per check and how ready each fund is.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:37,500
The total is not taken out of your plan for you. Compare it with Left after bills on the Dashboard.

6
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:44,000
Savings Goals works the same way for one-time targets.

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:51,500
Type a target, a target date and what is saved so far.

8
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:59,000
It counts the paychecks left and shows how much to set aside from each one.

9
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:07,500
The 2027 Overview tab shows your year by month. 3-paycheck months stand out.

10
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:15,000
Then keep the plan current with the weekly 15-minute checkup.

11
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Thanks for watching. A budgeting tool, not financial advice. Not tax or legal advice either.
